{"findings":[{"rule_id":"NM-002","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"Polyurethene"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"HARDENED 40-45 HRC"}],"comment":"The title block specifies the material as polyurethane (a polymer) yet also calls out a Rockwell C heat treatment of 40-45 HRC, which applies only to hardened metals. This contradiction will confuse manufacturing and inspection; the designer must remove or correct the heat treatment field for a plastic part."
    ,
    "recommended_correction":"Remove the heat treatment callout or replace it with a specification appropriate for polyurethane."}]}
